{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Share a Community Script Sample",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Let the generator do the setup",
      "description": "Open PowerShell 7 at the cloned repository root, where New-Sample.ps1 and scripts are located. Use a new, unused folder name; the generator rejects existing folders.\n\n```powershell\n.\\New-Sample.ps1 -ScriptFolderName \"spo-get-site-report\" `\n    -ScriptTitle \"Report SharePoint sites\" `\n    -ScriptShortDescription \"Export a SharePoint site inventory.\" `\n    -ScriptTool PnPPowerShell `\n    -AuthorFullName \"Your name\" `\n    -GitHubId \"your-github-handle\"\n```\n\nThe generator creates a README, sample.json, placeholder images, selected tool tabs, author details, and the final view tracker. It does not write or run your script. You still need to finish the documentation, select relevant products/categories, and replace example tool versions with tested ones.\n\nFor several tools, use comma-separated values such as PnPPowerShell,CliForMicrosoft365. All creates all eight supported tabs; remove any you do not implement. Follow docs/contributing/preparing-a-submission.md for the full checklist."
    },
    {
      "directory": "scripts/_template-script-submission",
      "title": "Prefer a manual starting point?",
      "description": "Copy this template into a new folder under scripts. Keep the template itself unchanged. Choose a descriptive lowercase name with a workload prefix and hyphens.\n\nRename assets/template.sample.json to assets/sample.json, fill in placeholders, and keep only the tools you implement. Replace assets/preview.png; the separate README screenshot assets/example.png is optional. No website build is needed to contribute."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/assets/template.sample.json",
      "line": 3,
      "title": "Make the sample discoverable",
      "description": "In your copied sample, use the folder name as name. Fill in title and shortDescription with the task and expected result, not just the tool name. Replace folder/title placeholders in the sample and preview URLs too. Keep the one-record JSON array."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/assets/template.sample.json",
      "line": 11,
      "title": "Use meaningful dates",
      "description": "Use yyyy-MM-dd dates. The generator fills these in for a new sample. When improving an existing sample, preserve creationDateTime and update updateDateTime for your change."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/assets/template.sample.json",
      "line": 13,
      "title": "Choose relevant products",
      "description": "Remove products that are not used by your sample; do not leave the whole template list. Use Microsoft Copilot as that product's name. Products describe the workload; tools and versions belong in metadata."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/assets/template.sample.json",
      "line": 24,
      "title": "Record the tools you tested",
      "description": "Keep metadata entries for the tools your sample actually supports. Replace example version numbers, including generator defaults, with the versions you tested. Keep matching reference links to each tool's documentation."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/assets/template.sample.json",
      "line": 70,
      "title": "Choose scenarios and commands",
      "description": "Keep only relevant categories, such as Report, Configure, or Security. Add command names and useful topics to tags so someone can find the sample by the task or command they know."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/assets/template.sample.json",
      "line": 84,
      "title": "Replace the preview",
      "description": "Replace assets/preview.png with a readable image representing your scenario. Check the thumbnail URL and describe the image in alt text. Remove tenant and personal information from screenshots."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/assets/template.sample.json",
      "line": 92,
      "title": "Credit everyone who helped",
      "description": "Verify your name, GitHub account, and picture URL. Add coauthors and keep the README contributor list consistent. A company or social account is not required."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/README.md",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Explain the scenario",
      "description": "In your copied README, use a clear title and summary. Remove the helper note and template text. Describe prerequisites, permissions, and the expected result. The README screenshot is optional; remove its reference if you do not use it."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/README.md",
      "line": 15,
      "title": "Add the tested script",
      "description": "Replace each <your script> placeholder with a complete implementation. Keep only the tool tabs you support and their shared documentation includes. Use safe example values, not credentials or private tenant details. Put an explicit impact warning before destructive operations."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/README.md",
      "line": 89,
      "title": "Preserve attribution and the disclaimer",
      "description": "If adapting another project, keep source credit and replace the example link with the actual source. Otherwise remove the example section. Credit all authors and keep the disclaimer. The generator's -KeepSourceCredit switch retains this section but does not choose the right link for you."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/_template-script-submission/README.md",
      "line": 101,
      "title": "Keep the tracker last, then share",
      "description": "The README's final line must be the visitor-tracking image. Replace {script-path} with the repository-relative sample directory, for example scripts/spo-get-site-report, using / separators. Preserve existing accessibility attributes. The generator fills this URL for you.\n\nTest your sample and open a focused pull request with the scenario and test details. Maintainers can help with finishing touches. After your first accepted sample, opt in at https://pnp.github.io/recognitionprogram/ to earn your Script Samples contributor badge. See docs/contributing/recognition.md for claiming and sharing it."
    }
  ],
  "ref": "main"
}
